---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Simple from "../../layouts/Simple.astro";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles", ({ data }) => data.section === "alternatives")).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);
const description =
  "Google Analytics, Amplitude, PostHog, Mixpanel, Plausible, and Fathom alternatives, compared by the job a founder actually needs done.";
---
<Simple
  title="Analytics alternatives"
  description={description}
  kicker="Alternatives"
  lede="Each guide below compares several tools. DataFast is the pick when you need revenue attribution. It is not the pick when you need a product-analytics suite."
  crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Alternatives" }]}
>
  <p>An “alternative” is only useful if you name the job you are leaving. Founders usually mean one of three jobs: a lighter report than GA4, a privacy-first traffic script, or a product suite that can replace Amplitude, Mixpanel, or PostHog. Those are different shortlists.</p>
  <p>DataFast belongs on the first and second lists when the question is which channel or page brought a payment. PostHog, Mixpanel, and Amplitude belong on the third list. Plausible and Fathom belong on the privacy-first traffic list, with revenue features that are real but not the whole product. The guides below keep those lines visible, with public prices checked on 24 November 2026.</p>
  <p>Start with the tool you have today, then read the sibling guides and the <a href="/reviews/datafast/">DataFast review</a> before you migrate. The <a href="/pricing/">pricing hub</a> and the <a href="/compare/posthog-vs-google-analytics/">PostHog vs GA4 comparison</a> sit next to these pages on purpose.</p>
  <section slot="wide" class="band band-yellow">
    <div class="article-wide">
      <h2>Guides in this section</h2>
      <div class="guides">
        {articles.map((article) => (
          <a class="guide" href={`/${article.id}/`}>
            <span class="type">Alternatives</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{article.data.title}</h3>
              <p>{article.data.description}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="meta">{`/${article.id}/`}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Simple>
